  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_9226997034364eb9b148a34270defeae",
      "statement": "On this host a graceful-shutdown drain unit stops every container to `Exited (0)` on shutdown, so boot never begins from \"containers were running\"; consequently `restart: unless-stopped` cannot recover them (it declines to restart a container that was already stopped when the daemon starts), and `restart: always` is required on every long-running prod service, enforced by `scripts/check-prod-restart-policy.mjs`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/prod-reboot-resilience.md#L106-L110",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a463ce007676f3021ea3366912699baa8815f9e988f27e49168c6d4ebdc2f9f6:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/check-prod-restart-policy.mjs#L1-L23",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:52c8d65b37bf0195a81acf73e8fbded52ffc6adfdb16c349593e1f36d51c4552:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4ec483475c424d7e8851851fc8cba34e",
      "statement": "A published port scoped to the tailnet IP silently fails to bind when the rootless daemon starts before the tailnet interface: the container reports `Up` with an empty Ports column and nothing listening, and only a `0.0.0.0` bind or a full rootless-daemon restart after the interface exists recovers it — a plain container restart does not.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/keycloak/compose.prod.yaml#L45-L53",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0e6c3cfc51950e9abe258258e6cf0961e4b42e8b888badc7710511a0e8d6a80e:"
        },
        {
