    {
      "id": "claim_7f2dc6dd392949038ae0a07c53b04e47",
      "statement": "The Mongo replica-set keyfile entrypoint writes the keyfile at mode `0400`; on a plain container restart the prior run's read-only file persists and non-root `mongod` cannot reopen it, so the container crash-loops. The entrypoint now removes the file before rewriting it on every start, making the operation idempotent, and its regression test must run as a non-root uid or it masks the bug.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/mc-service/mongo-entrypoint.sh#L13-L29",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:410f1f23a4d0a0a3f62b4753d3ed7be6f2bc9a8c069d4d0e30ff1256f986ddc4:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/mc-service/mongo-entrypoint.test.sh#L36-L46",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:814b97e66dd48e086c9fc67184f32d987642a1e66f561e999e1c3c0bd0b7bb18:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_94cffb0bc2b2466aaebd3204876350f4",
      "statement": "After a reboot `keycloak-service` can come back missing a shared external network attachment, breaking its consumers' DNS resolution of it; the durable remediation is a Komodo `prod-auth` redeploy (which recreates the container with its full declared network set) rather than a manual `docker network connect`, which the next reboot can lose.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/prod-reboot-resilience.md#L112-L118",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:97b80d13180752f75198e43d3a99a021060d28fb58883897ac6cf376bbba857e:"
        },
