          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1527a42e785d85947766159da6635c84b6ed5843b23bbc0ab7352ce919842d0c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bfc0018b18d2434fac0e2a0a259cc7bc",
      "statement": "The intra-stack Keycloak↔Postgres `keycloak-network` is compose-managed rather than external, so compose creates it and attaches both services atomically on every `up`; this closed the worse failure where a rolled-back port bind left Keycloak detached from all networks and unable to resolve its own Postgres.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/prod-reboot-resilience.md#L112-L118",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:97b80d13180752f75198e43d3a99a021060d28fb58883897ac6cf376bbba857e:"
