    {
      "id": "claim_aa351628fc0e4e209e9d27be3b3e7383",
      "statement": "Komodo periphery's `root_directory` default of `/etc/komodo` sits on a per-daemon tmpfs under rootless Docker (RootlessKit `--copy-up=/etc`), so the cloned repo checkout that every stack's relative bind-mounts resolve against is wiped on every reboot; Docker then auto-creates each missing bind-mount source file as a directory, and the Mongo and Vault containers fail with `not a directory … mount a directory onto a file` (exit 127).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/prod-reboot-resilience.md#L154-L168",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:10057f2bc65bff64d8d2d36b37309f0f9a5a246885e25d2a925f077504147c26:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/mc-service/compose.prod.yaml#L43-L44",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d0e8898c0de25dba988845769e5edfa6703b2424007361afbfbb7614f131e6c7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a98ef8160899414089062e992c9e4cbf",
      "statement": "The periphery root fix is host state: `PERIPHERY_ROOT_DIRECTORY` must point at a path on persistent disk and periphery must be recreated, and the server-setup runbook Phase 9 now bootstraps that value so a host rebuild cannot reintroduce `/etc/komodo`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/Server-Setup-Runbook.md#L846-L852",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e97a152aa2dee73d2e4909e4687ba19a29338ecb19a68bd98b176e6a4c0314c1:"
