    {
      "id": "claim_12684ae78cc544b5854fd7688dde7b37",
      "statement": "The restart-policy durability comes from the committed compose value plus the host-compose edits, not from the interim `docker update --restart always` applied over running containers — that update is lost the moment each container is next recreated by a Komodo redeploy, a compose `up`, or a host rebuild.",
      "evidence": [
